{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggZHoB3QsBuQK29NNRQC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fit gives Dq ≈ 1449 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 599 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 2760 cm⁻¹. Dq and B come from the three spin-allowed bands. C comes from the sharp spin-forbidden band and is an estimate.\n\n**Dq.** For d³ in an octahedral field, the lowest spin-allowed band ⁴A₂g→⁴T₂g equals Δ exactly. So 10Dq = 14 490 cm⁻¹ and Dq = 1449 cm⁻¹.\n\n**B.** The two upper spin-allowed bands, ⁴A₂g→⁴T₁g(F) and ⁴A₂g→⁴T₁g(P), come from a 2×2 mixing of the two ⁴T₁g terms. Their sum depends only on Δ and B:\n\nν₂ + ν₃ = 3Δ + 15B\n\n52 460 = 43 470 + 15B, so B ≈ 599 cm⁻¹.\n\nI checked this against the band separation. The required value is ν₃ − ν₂ = √(225B² + Δ² − 18BΔ), which gives 11 598 cm⁻¹. The observed separation is 11 600 cm⁻¹, so the fit is consistent.\n\n**C.** The sharp band at 12 710 cm⁻¹ is the ⁴A₂g→²Eg(a) transition, which lies just below ²T₁g. To a first approximation its energy is about 9B + 3C − 90B²/Δ, which gave C ≈ 3180 cm⁻¹. That formula is only approximate, so I used a full ligand-field diagonalization at Dq = 1449 cm⁻¹ and B = 599.3 cm⁻¹ instead.\n\n- At C = 3000 cm⁻¹, the full calculation puts ²Eg at 13 424 cm⁻¹. It also puts ⁴T₂g at 14 490 cm⁻¹, ⁴T₁g(a) at 20 432 cm⁻¹ and ⁴T₁g(b) at 32 028 cm⁻¹, matching the three observed spin-allowed bands.\n- The ²Eg energy changes by roughly 3 cm⁻¹ for each 1 cm⁻¹ change in C. I did not rerun the calculation at the final C. I estimated it by linear scaling, so it is good to roughly ±10 cm⁻¹.\n- Matching 12 710 cm⁻¹ therefore needs C lower by about 240 cm⁻¹, which gives C ≈ 2760 cm⁻¹ (C/B ≈ 4.6).\n\nI also tried the automated fitter. It gave a poor fit (B ≈ 310 cm⁻¹, RMSE ≈ 400 cm⁻¹) because it matched all four bands against every calculated level. I did not use that result.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1449, \"B\": 599, \"C\": 2760, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq and B follow exactly from the three spin-allowed bands, and C comes from fitting the lowest spin-forbidden ²Eg band.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2210,"cache_read_input_tokens":10260,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2210,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9453453-e666-4fd6-b825-2b5aa1410923","uuid":"59f54904-1e0a-4bb7-a1c3-03d4ae58843e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:36:38.459Z","request_id":"req_011CggZHnpi3vwcXajSwLxyc"}
